{"q":"145","t":"Binary Tree Postorder Traversal","d":"Easy","p":false,"c":"<p>Given the <code>root</code> of a&nbsp;binary tree, return <em>the postorder traversal of its nodes&#39; values</em>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">root = [1,null,2,3]</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">[3,2,1]</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"/assets/img/302bbb22b40631ca.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 264px;\" /></p>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">root = [1,2,3,4,5,null,8,null,null,6,7,9]</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">[4,6,7,5,2,9,8,3,1]</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"/assets/img/1c2fff4664fdf9e0.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 286px;\" /></p>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 3:</strong></p>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">root = []</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">[]</span></p>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 4:</strong></p>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">root = [1]</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">[1]</span></p>\n</div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>The number of the nodes in the tree is in the range <code>[0, 100]</code>.</li>\n\t<li><code>-100 &lt;= Node.val &lt;= 100</code></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<strong>Follow up:</strong> Recursive solution is trivial, could you do it iteratively?","h":[],"m":"{\r\n  \"name\": \"postorderTraversal\",\r\n  \"params\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"root\",\r\n      \"type\": \"TreeNode\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"return\": {\r\n    \"type\": \"list<integer>\",\r\n    \"dealloc\": true\r\n  }\r\n}","g":[{"name":"Stack","slug":"stack"},{"name":"Tree","slug":"tree"},{"name":"Depth-First Search","slug":"depth-first-search"},{"name":"Binary Tree","slug":"binary-tree"}],"s":[{"t":"Binary Tree Inorder Traversal","s":"binary-tree-inorder-traversal","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"N-ary Tree Postorder Traversal","s":"n-ary-tree-postorder-traversal","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Minimum Fuel Cost to Report to the Capital","s":"minimum-fuel-cost-to-report-to-the-capital","d":"Medium","p":false}],"co":[["Bloomberg","bloomberg"],["Google","google"],["Meta","facebook"],["Amazon","amazon"]],"cs":{"a":[],"b":[["Bloomberg","bloomberg",2]],"m":[["Google","google",9],["Amazon","amazon",7],["Meta","facebook",6],["Microsoft","microsoft",2]]}}